SUMMARY:Moth Night 2026
DESCRIPTION:The Bohart Museum of Entomology is hosting Moth Night 2026 on July 18th from 7 PM-10 PM. There is additional blacklighting in the Shields Oak Grove in the UCD Arboretum from 9:30 PM-11:30 PM\, led by entomologist Joel Hernandez. Experts will teach about life cycles\, adaptations\, and biodiversity of moths. This event is completely free with free parking\, and all ages are welcome!
URL:https://thedirt.online/event/moth-night-2026/
LOCATION:Academic Surge Building\, Room 1124\, 455 Crocker Lane\, Davis\, CA 95616\, Academic Surge Building\, Room 1124\, 455 Crocker Lane\, Davis\, CA\, 95616\, United States
CATEGORIES:Bring the Kids,Outside,Science
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://thedirt.online/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/MOTH-NIGHT-2026.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Bohart Museum of Entomology":MAILTO:bmuseum@ucdavis.edu
END:VEVENT
