BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Davis Downtown": "https://davisdowntown.com/event/the-wisdom-of-the-odyssey-with-phil-cousineau-book-talk-signing/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:davis_downtown
SUMMARY:The Wisdom of the Odyssey with Phil Cousineau - Book Talk & Signin
 g
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260719T133000
UID:10002096-1784462400-1784467800@davisdowntown.com
DESCRIPTION:Join The Wardrobe\, in partnership with Avid Reader Bookstor
 e and The Varsity Theatre\, for a special afternoon with acclaimed autho
 r\, filmmaker\, and storyteller Phil Cousineau as he discusses his newes
 t book\, The Wisdom of the Odyssey. \nTimed with the opening weekend of C
 hristopher Nolan’s highly anticipated film inspired by Homer’s epic\, 
 this engaging conversation explores the deeper wisdom and timeless themes 
 of The Odyssey: the journey that changes everything. \n🗓 Sunday\, Jul
 y 19\, 2026⏰ 12:00 PM – 1:30 PM📍 Varsity Theatre616 Second Street
 \, Davis\, CA🎟 Free Admission \nFollowing the talk\, Phil Cousineau wi
 ll be available for a book signing\, with books available for purchase fr
 om Avid Reader Bookstore. \nAuthor of more than 40 books – including Th
 e Art of Pilgrimage and The Hero’s Journey: Joseph Campbell on His Lif
 e and Work. Cousineau is an internationally recognized writer\, teacher\, 
 filmmaker\, and cultural historian whose work explores mythology\, creativ
 ity\, and the human experience. \nThis event marks the first-ever book ta
 lk at the Varsity Theatre\, making it a memorable opportunity to experienc
 e literature in one of Davis’ most iconic venues. With seating limited t
 o 300 guests\, early arrival is encouraged. \nWhether you’re a lifelong 
 fan of The Odyssey\, excited to see Christopher Nolan’s new film\, or s
 imply looking for an inspiring afternoon of storytelling and conversation\
 , this free community event is not to be missed.
LOCATION:Varsity Theatre\, 616 Second Street\, Davis\, CA\, 95616
